<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Privileged permissions for the bundled F-Droid store.

    These belong to org.fdroid.fdroid.privileged, NOT to org.fdroid.fdroid.

    F-Droid's own manifest never declares INSTALL_PACKAGES or DELETE_PACKAGES;
    it asks only for REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES / REQUEST_DELETE_PACKAGES, the
    variants that prompt the user. Android grants a package only what that
    package requests, so allowlisting the install permissions against
    org.fdroid.fdroid granted nothing at all — F-Droid still fell back to
    SessionInstaller and raised the PackageInstaller confirmation UI for every
    install and every update.

    The package that does request them is the Privileged Extension, which
    exports org.fdroid.fdroid.privileged.IPrivilegedService for F-Droid's
    PrivilegedInstaller to bind. Both permissions below are signature|privileged
    in AOSP 13, so this allowlist is what lets a priv-app hold them.

    Note this product currently sets ro.control_privapp_permissions=log
    (fydroid_rt_common.mk), not enforce, and under log the check is both
    non-fatal and permissive: PermissionManagerServiceImpl ends it with
    `return !CONTROL_PRIVAPP_PERMISSIONS_ENFORCE`, so a missing entry is granted
    anyway with only a Slog.w, and the violations set that would abort boot is
    populated solely under enforce. The entry below therefore does not change
    behaviour today — it is what keeps the extension working on the day this
    product moves to enforce, which is the direction of travel. What actually
    fixes silent install today is shipping the extension apk at all.

    Nothing is listed for org.fdroid.fdroid: checked against
    frameworks/base/core/res/AndroidManifest.xml, every permission it requests
    is normal, dangerous, or signature-without-privileged (REQUEST_INSTALL_
    PACKAGES is signature|appop, MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE is
    signature|appop|preinstalled), and none of those are allowlisted here.
-->
<permissions>
    <privapp-permissions package="org.fdroid.fdroid.privileged">
        <permission name="android.permission.INSTALL_PACKAGES"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.DELETE_PACKAGES"/>
    </privapp-permissions>
</permissions>
